  <main class="content">
    <h1 id="introduction">Introduction</h1>

<p>Project Orion is an initiative to modernize data-driven decision-making across the organization by aligning systems, processes, and people around a common analytical foundation. This whitepaper summarizes the project's motivation, methods, and early results to inform leadership and stakeholders.</p>

<h2 id="background">Background</h2>

<p>Over the last five years, data volume and variety across our product lines have expanded dramatically. Legacy reporting pipelines and fragmented ownership led to duplicated efforts and inconsistent metrics. Orion proposes a unified analytics platform that standardizes data definitions, centralizes governance, and accelerates insight generation for both strategic and operational decisions.</p>

<h2 id="scope-and-objectives">Scope and Objectives</h2>

<ul>
<li>Establish a single source of truth for core business metrics.</li>
<li>Reduce reporting duplication and time-to-insight by 30–50%.</li>
<li>Provide transparent lineage and reproducibility for critical analyses.</li>
<li>Enable self-service exploration without compromising data quality or security.</li>
</ul>

<h1 id="methods">Methods</h1>

<p>The Orion program combined process redesign with platform engineering. We adopted a phased approach to de-risk delivery and keep feedback loops short while ensuring auditable, production-ready outputs.</p>

<h2 id="data-collection">Data Collection</h2>

<p>Data sources were cataloged and prioritized by impact and feasibility. Source systems included transactional databases, event streams, CRM records, and product telemetry. We implemented standardized ingestion using change data capture (CDC) where supported and batch extracts where not, with all feeds landing in a governed data lake.</p>

<p>Key practices:</p>

<ul>
<li>Automated schema detection and contract tests to prevent breaking changes.</li>
<li>Versioned datasets with immutable snapshots for reproducibility.</li>
<li>PII minimization and tokenization aligned to privacy policies.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="transformation-and-modeling">Transformation and Modeling</h2>

<p>Transformations followed a medallion (bronze → silver → gold) pattern. We used declarative pipelines with tests at each layer:</p>

<ul>
<li>Bronze: Raw ingestion with structural normalization only.</li>
<li>Silver: Conformed entities and slowly changing dimensions for consistent keys.</li>
<li>Gold: Curated, business-ready marts aligned with agreed metric definitions.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="analysis-and-validation">Analysis and Validation</h2>

<p>We established acceptance criteria jointly with stakeholders for each metric. Statistical validation and backtesting against historical baselines ensured that new pipelines matched or exceeded the accuracy of legacy reports. Where variance existed, we traced lineage to root causes and documented remediation.</p>

<h1 id="results">Results</h1>

<p>Orion's initial rollout covered finance, sales, and product analytics. Early outcomes indicate meaningful improvements in consistency, agility, and confidence across reporting workflows.</p>

<h2 id="key-findings">Key Findings</h2>

<ul>
<li>Metric alignment reduced conflicting reports by 72% in covered domains.</li>
<li>Report production time for monthly business reviews decreased from 4 days to 1.5 days.</li>
<li>Data quality incidents declined as schema contract violations were caught pre-production.</li>
<li>Stakeholders reported higher trust in dashboards due to transparent definitions and lineage.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="illustrative-outcomes">Illustrative Outcomes</h2>

<p>Analysts used the conformed data model to expose a hidden churn driver in a previously siloed telemetry feed, enabling a targeted retention campaign that lifted 30-day retention by 2.1 percentage points in pilot cohorts.</p>

<h2 id="next-steps">Next Steps</h2>

<p>We plan to extend coverage to marketing and support domains, implement real-time features for operational alerts, and expand self-service tooling with governed semantic layers. Continuous feedback and metric governance councils will maintain alignment as the platform scales.</p>

